(China Daily reporter Yan Huan)
The fitness industry must overcome the trust crisis - China News
Another big gym with a thunderstorm?
Recently, the member rights protection issue of the famous fitness institution Zhongjian Fitness has attracted the attention of the society.
After the Spring Festival, many members found that their stores were not in normal operation. Subsequently, rumors about the bankruptcy and running away of the institution caused the members to panic, and the public security and human resources departments intervened.
Finally, the relevant person in charge of the institution made a statement, promising to do their best to protect the legitimate rights and interests of employees and members. The incident was then finally settled.
The first reaction of many members is that the problem is not a big deal, because some stores in individual gyms have problems, they are temporarily closed, and consumers should be calm and wait for the problem to be solved.
Behind the fitness club membership dispute is an underlying issue of industry trust crisis.
Traditional gyms in China generally adopt a prepaid model, and the bottom line of its development is to "earn money from users who do not come".
By selling pre-sale memberships to obtain cash flow, opening new stores continuously, it seems that it can be cyclical, but in fact it is eating the grain of the ox, and it is impossible to form a stable profit model.
Negative publicity about fitness centers and other industries is frequently circulating, severely undermining consumer confidence.
From a market perspective, gyms can certainly be considered a good business opportunity.
The fitness market is cyclical but remains under capital attention.
Multiple data show that interest in cultural and entertainment consumption is on the rise, with the market showing signs of recovery.
Specific to the fitness market, with steady improvement in residents' living standards and widespread acceptance of healthy-living concepts, there is great potential for growth in the industry.
The better the situation, the more the industry needs to focus on quality of development.
However, some institutions are overly optimistic about the fitness market after the recovery of consumption. They are just out of the crisis and are eager to expand their businesses by investing all the funds in building new stores.
Undoubtedly, over the past few years due to the impact of the epidemic, many institutions have withdrawn from the market, and industry restructuring has occurred. Strong enterprises at this time choosing to increase their acquisition efforts and reposition themselves is not necessarily a missed opportunity.
However, in order for the fitness market to develop in a healthy way and enter a virtuous circle, the industry must change its traditional mode of operation and change its operating strategy.
Only by consolidating and improving the consumer's trust and security can we truly win the market and win the future.
Rather than building new stores to capture market share, the fitness industry needs to focus on improving service quality and achieving sustainable growth to stabilize users.
First, it is necessary to rely on service to retain users.
The gym is a service industry, which is essentially user-oriented and focuses on improving the quality of service.
Secondly, it is necessary to improve user experience through digital transformation.
For example, the current popular model of internet fitness gyms, where users pay per session and choose their own facilities.
At the same time, body data, movement data can be used effectively and can also meet social needs, enabling a complete service loop from online to offline.
Without private sales and large annual memberships, users’ concerns about gyms “running away” have been reduced, and their trust has also been improved.
Moreover, it is necessary to explore and develop diversified business models.
Today, sports consumption is moving from single-service to scenario-based consumption, with fitness clubs poised to become new entry points for consumption. Products and services related to physical exercise such as supplements and fitness equipment may become new revenue sources, offering consumers more choices.
Jiang Tianjiao
Buy at a discount!
Nanjing real estate market again shows "price compensation" - China News
Yangzi Evening News (reporter Ma Chubo) reported on October 10 that the reporter found out that the “guaranteed price agreement” that had not been seen for more than ten years had returned to the Nanjing real estate market. A property developer in Nanjing claimed that the “difference compensation” in the property was more than the discounts of other properties before the delivery of the property, and the developer was willing to exchange the property and return the difference.
The "Guaranteed Value Agreement" conditions aren't few.
This residential project located in Jiangbei New District is called Baoji Yanzhong Cuiyun Tai and Mr. Sun, who came to view it last weekend, told reporters that he had noticed an announcement while touring the site.
The developer sent the pictures to the reporter, which showed that the developer promised that if the buyer purchased the property between February 1st and February 28th, the developer would exchange the property for another property with a better discount (limited to the same unit type, the same building, the same unit type, and the same property type of the same property) and refund the difference.
Mr. Sun said that the sales consultant explained that this was just an “insurance agreement” – to give buyers peace of mind when they sell and not worry about developers lowering their prices for promotional purposes. "Now I’m afraid that once we buy it, it will be lowered in price anyway; going to the sales office to protest won’t leave me time to do so, and if I don’t protest, it’s really nice."
There are still many homebuyers who believe that “price guarantee agreements,” while reassuring buyers with their assurances, come at a high price.
Ms. Zheng, who is planning to buy a starter home in Nanchang, said that properties with price protection were first limited to the same floor plan and had to be located on the same building block as well as within the same unit. Buyers could not compare prices easily, so the “barrier” was still quite high.
There are also buyers who believe that because of information asymmetry, salespeople may offer additional concessions without disclosing them to customers, making it difficult for buyers to seek redress.
Is it possible to retain home buyers remains to be seen.
The reporter found on the Nanjing online real estate website that the property was sold out in November last year with two towers of 252 units. The floor area of the units is 105 square meters, 114 square meters, and 129 square meters, and the sales price of the fully furnished units is 39,843 yuan per square meter.
However, over the past two months, online real estate shows that the total number of unsold units in the complex is currently 157 units, accounting for 62.3%, of which 128 units are in the 8th floor, 113 units are in the 7th floor, and 44 out of 124 units are not sold, and the total number of completed projects is only 33 units, accounting for only 13%.
Market participants note that “price protection agreements” were also in place in Nanjing in 2008.
In August of the previous year, the cross-Shan-Hu residential complex, Xiangtang West Garden, in Huangshan Road, attracted buyers' attention with its "Guaranteed Price Plan," which stipulated that if there was an increase in project discounts within one year, the company would refund any shortfall to existing residents.
In April 2011, Nanjing also had nine projects that promised “price compensation” for some of their units.
"Real estate is on the mend; now it needs a ‘shot in the arm.’"
Mr. Shen, a senior operator in the Nanjing real estate industry, said that the price caps are also one of the marketing methods of the company.
He believes that today developers need more confidence than buyers, and that the introduction of a price-fixing agreement is actually giving them a boost.
Whether it is possible to retain buyers depends on multiple factors such as policy regulation and loan thresholds; at present, this remains to be seen.
Chinese rescue team continues rescue operation in Turkey, rescuing 4 trapped people - Xinhua
According to the Ministry of Emergency Management website, on February 10, the Chinese rescue team, which is searching Turkey, sent three operations teams, 45 rescue workers and rescued one trapped person.
At the same time, two search and evaluation groups were sent to evaluate and check the 15 buildings on Vodabashi Street.
So far, 4 people were rescued and 5 others found dead; assessments of life signs and risks have been made for 25 collapsed buildings.
The rescue team will continue to carry out in-depth rescue operations, adapting the rescue force scientifically and according to the actual situation in the disaster area and the situation on the ground.
The rescue team obtained information on assistance requests through multiple channels such as embassies, local governments, and UN relief organizations, verified them through various means including online inquiries and on-site searches.
Introduce the current rescue environment and building collapse to the Chinese Hong Kong Rescue Team, and jointly carry out search operations.
Currently, the team is coordinating with the Italian rescue team (SSC5), and has three staff members working in the Regional Rescue Coordination Center 5, communicating with the teams in Italy, the United Kingdom, Serbia, Slovakia, Oman and other countries, and learning about the work of the United Nations and the rescue teams of the countries.
The rescue team continuously strengthens safety management and personnel support, adhering to the principle of unified command and prioritizing safety, enhancing on-site safety control, strengthening work discipline requirements, and clearly defining safety precautions.
Implement continuous duty and watchkeeping systems to strengthen camp area security.
The medical staff of the rescue team provide health check-ups to their members every day and strengthen the medical protection for key personnel. The entire rescue team is currently healthy and has been conducting camp area disinfection.
After the establishment of the camp, the logistics security team built 26 field tents of 4 types, such as command communication, equipment storage, medical cleaning, living accommodation and dog houses, to ensure more than 30 sets of rescue equipment on the ground.
Kim Jong-un and his daughter are very close, his wife is left out
(Reuters) North Korea held its 75th anniversary military parade on August 8 evening, with Kim Yo Jong, daughter of leader Kim Jong Un, attending and standing alongside her father at the podium.
On the 9th day of the month, the Korean Central News Agency released a video showing Kim Jong-un hugging his father and talking to him in a low voice. She often looked at him with a loving gaze and touched his chest. The father-daughter interaction was broadcast throughout the country.
But the first lady, Li Xue, had to take a back seat.
According to reports from “Korean Central News Agency” and others, Kim Jong-nam and Ri Sol-ju were seen at an official photo of their daughter Kim Jung-a attending a banquet on July 7th. Kim Jung-a was not only rarely sitting in the middle C position with her parents but also joined Kim Jong-nam together with him on the podium for the military parade celebrating the 75th anniversary of建军节.
The Central Television of North Korea released the video of the parade after the event, revealing more scenes of father-daughter love.
Kim Jong-nam frequently looked at his daughter from the podium and never lost their smiles; they also whispered to each other in hushed tones. Kim Chol-ae once cupped her father’s cheeks with both hands, while Kim Jong-nam reciprocated with a radiant smile.
Other official media footage also showed Kim's mother, Ai, touching her father's face while sitting on the sofa with Kim Jong-un in the living room; she was holding hands while walking with her father and touching Kim Jong-un's chest.
The first lady, Li Xue, was always behind or sitting in the side, and she was always a few steps away from her husband and daughter.
According to Korean media, since the first time he appeared in public after the launch of the first 17-rocket missile on November 18 last year, the exposure probability of Kim Jong-un has been increasing, and he has appeared five times in official occasions.
The official North Korean media used titles such as "my dearest son" and "my noble son" to refer to Kim Jong-un, and broadcast footage of Kim Jong-un repeatedly shouting his death oath to the white blooded while watching the parade from the stands.
These signs have raised doubts about whether Kim Jong-un has been predetermined as the heir to the Kim dynasty, and the Washington Post analysis said "this is a signal that Kim Jong-un is pushing his daughter to the position of the next leader at a young age." However, some opinions believe that it is too early to make such judgments, as there are various possibilities in the situation where Kim Jong-un has a son.
Xinhua Commentator: Promoting China’s Modernization is a Systematic Project – Four Commentaries on Deeply Understanding the Keynote Address of General Secretary Xi Jinping at the Opening Ceremony of the Study Session on Learning and Implementing the Spirit of the 20th CPC National Congress - China News Service
Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, February 11 (Zhang Ying) - The article is entitled: Promoting the Chinese Modernization is a Systematic Work - Four Thoughts on Deeply Understanding the Important Speech of General Secretary Xi Jinping at the Opening Ceremony of the Study Session on Learning and Implementing the Spirit of the 20th CPC National Congress
Xinhua News Agency commentator
The promotion of Chinese modernization is a systemic project that requires a combination of coordination, systematic planning, holistic promotion, and the correct handling of a number of important relationships such as top-level design and practice exploration, strategy and strategy, integrity and innovation, efficiency and fairness, vitality and order, self-reliance and openness.
At the opening session of the study class for new members of the Central Committee, alternate members, and main leaders at provincial and ministerial levels who have been newly admitted to the Central Committee, President Xi Jinping scientifically grasped the laws of modernization construction, deeply systematized and comprehensively expounded on a series of major relationships that need to be handled in practice, providing scientific methodology for us to accelerate China’s modernization.
The promotion of China’s modernization involves various fields such as economy, politics, culture, society, and ecological civilization, touching on aspects like governance, national defense, internal security, and foreign policy. It requires both systematic planning and bold innovation to achieve comprehensive advancement.
To design an overarching strategy requires deep insight into the world’s development trends and accurate grasp of the common aspirations of the people. It also involves in-depth exploration of economic and social development laws to ensure that the planning and policy system reflects its timeliness, adheres to laws, and is innovative. The plan should be coherent both far and near, harmonize top-down with bottom-up, and coordinate content.
Advancing China’s modernization is an exploratory venture that involves many unknown territories and requires bold exploration in practice through innovation and reform to drive development progress, not clinging to ancient methods or waiting for opportunities to come.
Strategic issues are the fundamental issues of a political party and a country.
To advance China’s modernization model, we must enhance strategic foresight to foresee and lead the future with scientific strategic vision; strengthen global strategy to address major issues that affect the rise and fall of the country’s cause and its overall development; and ensure stability in our strategies so they can be implemented consistently over time and achieved successfully.
To scientifically grasp the dialectical unity of strategy and tactics, integrate their principles with their flexibility, be flexible and adaptable, respond to changes in circumstances, and make decisions on the spot, seize opportunities, and gain strategic initiative in accordance with local conditions, situational considerations, and favorable trends.
The Chinese people are a nation of integrity and innovation.
We must handle the relationship between upholding and innovating well, and ensure that we uphold the essence and source, the root and soul of China’s modernization, and ensure that China’s modernization is on the right track, while also putting innovation in a prominent position in the national development overall plan, responding to the requirements of the times, focusing on the major theoretical and practical issues, actively seeking changes and adjustments, and vigorously promoting reform and innovation, so as to continuously create new momentum and advantages for development, and fully unleash the creativity of the whole society.
Efficiency is an important basis for fairness, and fairness is a strong guarantee of efficiency.
We advance China’s modernization model, both creating higher efficiency than capitalism and more effectively maintaining social equity, achieving an integration of efficiency and equity that is mutually reinforcing and unified.
Handle efficiency and equity well, continuously realizing that development serves the people, is for the people, and benefits the people, so that modernization achievements can be enjoyed more equitably by all the people.
To advance China’s modernization model, it is necessary to handle the relationship between vitality and order, ensuring that society remains both dynamic and orderly.
To effectively balance development and security, we must uphold the overall national security perspective, strengthen the national security system, enhance capabilities for maintaining national security, and resolutely safeguard state sovereignty, regime safety, ideological security, and the security of key areas.
We should consider more security factors in the process of development, and enhance the national security strength through development, and use the development results to consolidate the foundation of national security. We should also create a favorable security environment for economic and social development, constantly stimulate the development potential, and achieve a good interaction between high-quality development and high-level security.
To advance China’s modernization model, we must both adhere to our own path and broaden our world perspective; we should also uphold openness to the outside world, continuously expanding the breadth and depth of China’s modernization model.
To persist in independence and self-reliance, and to uphold placing our country and nation’s development at the core of our own strength; and to firmly grasp the destiny of our country's progress and prosperity within ourselves.
We should continuously expand our opening to the outside world, deeply participate in global industrial division and cooperation, make good use of both domestic and international resources, expand the development space for China’s modernization with win-win cooperation, and create a better future together.
Follow the path to achieve far-reaching goals.
Let us, under the strong leadership of the Central Party, with Comrade Xi Jinping at its core, and under the guidance of the socialist ideology and science of the Chinese New Age, grasp the rule of law, persevere, be active, proactive, creative, and properly handle a series of important relationships, and continue to advance on the new path of building a comprehensive socialist modern state, continuously opening up new frontiers of Chinese modernity.
Together to resist the CPC, the US, Japan and the Philippines reached a consensus on defense
Asia - On February 9, Philippine President Bongbong Marcos visited Japan and met with Prime Minister Fumio Kishida.
The two sides agreed to oppose the Chinese invasion of the South China Sea and the East China Sea, and the leaders of the Philippines and Japan issued a joint statement after the meeting, saying that they would conduct substantial defense exchanges with the United States through the signing of a three-way defense agreement and oppose the hegemonic policy of the Chinese Communist Party.
According to Japanese media reports, Kishida hopes that this meeting will help Japan and the Philippines establish policies for dealing with the crisis in the Taiwan Strait.
Marcos Jr. visited China in early January and was awarded a $20 billion deal.
But since then, relations between China and the Philippines have not only not improved but have actually deteriorated.
Last month, the Philippines signed an agreement with the US to open up more bases for American forces and secure the South China Sea’s security.
The newly added base is located 300 km from Taiwan and is also one of the closest to China.
If there is a crisis in Taiwan, US forces may launch operations from bases in the Philippines.
Japanese media have noted that Japan, South Korea, Taiwan, and the Philippines now form an axis with the US to build a “counter-Chinese arc” in the Western Pacific region for regional cooperation.
China Encourages High Fertility Rates and Recruits Donors to Universities for Quality Testing
The Human Sperm Bank of Yunnan Province, China, on Monday launched a campaign to ask people with a college degree or higher or a student to donate sperm from 8 to 12 times to receive a subsidy of 4,500 yuan.
Taiwan media reported today that this message had risen to the top of Weibo’s hot search list and sparked initiatives from many provinces including Zhejiang, Shaanxi, Hubei, Shandong, and Beijing.
According to a report by the Free Times, China encourages university students to donate sperm.
The donor requirements for different universities are different. The donor requirements for Beijing University are the highest. In addition to the academic requirements, the donor must be taller than 1.70 meters, have a good appearance, no obvious hair loss, and the near vision degree cannot be higher than 600 degrees.
The report says that the Yunnan Human Sperm Bank states that donors can receive a complete male reproductive system examination worth 1,000 RMB, including semen and karyotype analysis, which is rarely done by most people, with great significance for understanding their fertility status.
Donors must meet the following criteria: height over 165 cm, bachelor's degree or higher education level (or currently enrolled), no color blindness or color weakness, and no genetic diseases such as hepatitis B.
The report quotes a message from China’s Tianmu News that says there is an advertisement in the sperm bank of Shaanxi province which reads “donating sperm for money and infinite glory.” It calls on young people to donate their sperm and encourages netizens to forward related information so as to spread love.
Prices in Shaanxi exceed those in Yunnan; donors who qualify can receive RMB 300 cash per time, and those who donate sperm for a certain number of times will be given an additional RMB 5000 subsidy.
The highest known subsidy is in Beijing, at 5,150 yuan.
The E-account of the hedge fund is here: the SEC authorizes the development of all funds in the name of investors to be consolidated and consulted - Economic Observer Network - Professional financial news website
Economic Observer reporter Chen Shan How difficult is it to aggregate account information due to the proliferation of fund purchase channels?
Do you always forget your little treasure chest?
The problems of the Kievan people will soon be resolved.
On February 10, the SEC announced that the E-Account Funds Funds app was launched in mobile app stores and was open for testing.
It is reported that "Fund E Account" provides one-stop query services for individual investors to obtain information on public offering fund accounts and shares, aiming to address industry pain points such as forgetting account numbers and querying them in a cumbersome manner.
According to Wind data, as of the end of 2022, there are 156 public fund managers in the country, with a fund size of about 26 trillion yuan; 167 public fund share registration agencies, 411 public fund sales agencies.
The accounting systems of the different quota registries are independent of each other and lack a unified industry-wide query channel.
Industry observers say that at the end of 2021, there were over 72 million fund investors in China, meaning that half of the country’s population had invested in funds.
Previously, investors had to query their purchase status through different sales institutions; now they can view all of their purchases on the “Fund E Account,” which makes it easy to see their holdings.
What is the "Fund E Account" APP?
According to the relevant documents, the "Fund E Account" APP is a mobile application developed and built by China Clearing Co., Ltd. with the approval of the China Securities Regulatory Commission. It can provide one-stop query of the holdings of off-exchange public fund products for investors.
Investors can conveniently and efficiently track their holdings of all fund products offered by different managers through the “Fund E Account,” thereby significantly enhancing query efficiency.
Specifically, investors can query information about their fund accounts through the “Fund E Account,” including account information for funds opened at all public mutual fund managers and trading accounts opened at public fund sales institutions, as well as holdings of products such as open-end securities investment funds and collective asset management plans that do not have an upper limit on the number of investors.
Liu Yicheng, the business manager of Shanghai Securities Fund Evaluation Research Center, told the Economic Observer that investors can get to know their holdings of off-exchange public fund through the "Fund E Account" App, which can help them find "lost assets", and more importantly, it can help customers to collect comprehensive information of their fund investment in a unified account, which can help customers to better and more timely, accurate and complete grasp their own investment situation, and better optimize their fund portfolio, and better plan their own financial arrangements.
How to register?
Journalists have noted that the “Fund E Account” app has been made available on Huawei, Apple, Xiaomi, OPPO, and Vivo app stores but is still in public beta testing phase; users need to fill an invitation code during registration, and investors can contact their respective fund managers for assistance.
A customer service representative of a large public fund in Shanghai provided a 6-digit invitation code to the Economic Observer reporter and told the reporter, "During the trial operation of the APP, China Clearing provided a certain number of invitation codes to each fund management company. Investors can call to obtain them. We will provide them to investors.
After the trial run, the invitation code will no longer be used for open user registration.
“
Journalists registered and used their accounts according to instructions on the SEC’s “Fund E Account” website, completing the process in just minutes. The entire procedure involved four steps: user registration, real-name authentication, fund account binding, and public offering fund inquiry.
After completing this step of real-name authentication, clicking on the “Asset Fund Binding” button allows journalists to see all their purchased fund products from various fund sales platforms listed in the binding options (which can be linked to an account). After successful binding, they will be able to intuitively view their total investment in funds and start using the query function.
It is worth noting that the "Fund E Account" only provides query services to investors, and cannot conduct redemption and repurchase.
The data displayed in the "Fund E account" is generally the date of the user's query (T day) forwarded by three trading days.
For example, on February 10th, when you open the "Fund E Account," the total assets, fund shares, and net asset value displayed under the Asset page correspond to the date three trading days prior to that, which is February 7th.
