Multiple data points show poor start to year for Taiwan's economy - Xinhua News Agency
Shanghai-based Xinhua News Agency reported that exports reached “five black” in January, with the manufacturing Purchasing Managers’ Index (PMI) falling for seven consecutive months and consumer prices rising to the “three digits.” Taiwan’s authorities have recently released economic data for January 2023.
Experts say that Taiwan’s economy is underperforming in the new year and growth pressures are mounting.
According to the Ministry of Finance of Taiwan’s Treasury Affairs Bureau, Taiwan’s exports for January this year amounted to $31.51 billion, down 21.2% from last year and marking their fifth consecutive month of negative growth.
The exports of 11 major export categories declined in comparison to the same period last year.
The decline in plastics and rubber products and optical instruments was the deepest, at 37.6% and 35.7% respectively.
The export of electronic components fell by 20.1% year-on-year, the largest decline in 11 years.
Among them, the annual decline of integrated circuits was 18.3%, the biggest decline in 14 years.
Chai Mianna, the head of the Statistics Department, said that this showed that the weak demand for consumer electronics had spread, and the electronic industry was entering a correction period.
Statistics showed that the exports and imports of Taiwan region both decreased in January, with the export exceeding only 2.34 billion US dollars, the lowest level in the past three years.
The Taiwan authorities’ finance bureau believes that global terminal demand is declining, industrial adjustments in inventory will suppress manufacturers' purchasing intentions for materials, and export weakness may not improve temporarily. The Taiwanese first-quarter exports could be worse than expected this year.
According to the Taiwan Institute of China Economics, the Taiwan Manufacturing Purchasing Managers Index (PMI) in January this year was 40.4% seasonally adjusted, down 3.3 percentage points from December last year, a seven-month consecutive contraction.
The economic monitoring index system includes PMI, with 50% as the dividing line. If the index is above 50%, it means prosperity, and if it is below 50%, it means contraction.
The January Taiwan PMI's five indicators include new orders, production and labor contraction, lower supplier delivery times, and shrinking inventories.
All six industries have returned a PMI contraction, and the order of contraction is as follows: the electricity and machinery industry (35.1%), the electronic and optical industry (35.2%), the chemical and biotechnology industry (39.2%), the basic raw materials industry (42.4%), the transportation industry (42.6%) and the food and textile industry (45.7%).
On the price side, the CPI in Taiwan rose by 3.04% in January, breaking the 3% mark since July last year, according to the CPI's Directorate-General for Budget.
Among them, the price of vegetables rose by 28.25%, which was a 17-month high.
Cao Zhijian, a special commissioner of the General Administration of Taizhou, said that the increase in the price of vegetables was indeed higher than expected, excluding the Spring Festival factor, and that the average CPI in January and February should be close to 2.71 percent in December last year, and that inflation pressures remained high.
Looking ahead to Taiwan’s economy for this year, experts predict gloom in island media reports from Combined “United Daily News,” Yahoo Finance, and others.
Liu Daing, professor of the Department of Economics at Taipei Central University, said that the export recession could cause problems in the cash flow of export manufacturers and increase the risk of default.
At the same time, declining orders have forced manufacturers to cut labor costs, which in turn affects the labor market and household incomes, thereby undermining consumer spending power.
Chu Daosheng of the Institute for Taiwan Economic Research believes that inflation in Europe and America is not yet under control, with demand continuing to decline, and expects Taiwan’s exports to continue to contract until the second half of this year.
Taiwan’s economy is export-driven; its growth will be weaker than last year because of sluggish exports.
Did the Balloon Incident Brighten America's Eyes?
Strengthening restrictions on technology exports to China
The Wall Street Journal reported today that the United States is preparing to further tighten its technology exports to China after the balloon incident.
Current and former security officials said the balloon incident highlighted the national security threat posed by China and would seek more political support for strengthening U.S. technological protection.
The US claims that the balloon carried antennas and sensors for intelligence gathering and communications.
According to Martyn Rasser, a former senior CIA official who now works at the Washington think tank's Center for a New American Security.
This is undoubtedly fueling the hard-line view on China.
White House press secretary Karine Jean-Pierre told reporters Thursday that the U.S. will also consider taking broader action to expose and respond to China's larger-scale surveillance activities, which pose a threat to our national security and to our allies and partners.
The U.S. officials said they had notified the governments of more than 30 countries about the balloon incident and that international coordination was vital to counter the Chinese threat.
Senior researcher Emily Benson of the Center for Strategic and International Studies said that in addition to the actions of the Biden administration, the newly established U.S. House of Representatives U.S.-China Commission on Strategic Competition may pressure the United States to take more severe measures to slow down China's development.
She says that members of Congress will feel increasing pressure to take more assertive positions, which may in turn force the White House to adopt even stronger policies.
Many who advocate tighter export controls are also pushing for the scope of regulation to be expanded to include industries like artificial intelligence, the Wall Street Journal reported.
The US government is also developing a foreign investment review program to examine whether US investments abroad pose a potential national security threat from China.
Analysts say the White House may face calls for a faster launch of the plan.
The first individual pension products have been launched, with minimum holding period of 360 days - Xinhua News Agency
The first personal pension products are on sale
The 7 products offered by the home institution can be selected, with the shortest holding period being 360 days.
Personal pension investment products are finally available.
On February 10, China Finance Network released the first batch of personal pension fund management products. The personal pension fund management products of Agricultural Bank of China, Industrial and Commercial Bank of China and China Post Group officially went on sale.
At last, the “shelf” of personal pension accounts is complete with four products – personal pension savings, personal pension investment, personal pension insurance, and personal pension open-end funds.
It is reported that all of the first batch of individual pension products are open-ended net-value type public offerings, with 5 new issues and 2 existing ones; except for one product which is a mixed-type, the remaining six products are fixed-income types.
The reporter of Beijing Youth Daily saw that 4 of the 5 new products were from ICBC Wealth Management, all of which were fixed-income products with the shortest holding period of 365 days, 540 days, 720 days and 1080 days, and the corresponding performance benchmarks (annualized) were 3.70% - 4.20%, 4.10% - 4.60%, 4.40% - 4.90% and 5.25% - 5.75%, respectively.
The remaining new product is "Postal Bank Wealth Addition Hong Jing 1095 Days 1", a fixed-income product that started to raise funds on February 10 and ended on February 19. The risk level is two.
Of the two products still in existence, one is Agricultural Bank of China's "Agricultural Bank of China Centennial - Dynamic" 360-day Innovation and Technology RMB Wealth Management Product with a mix investment nature and a risk level of three.
The second ongoing product is “Post and Express Wealth Add Joy - Harmony Shortest Holding for 365 Days No. 1,” which is of fixed income type. It started fundraising on December 30 last year and officially began operations on January 4 this year. Its cumulative net asset value as of February 8 was 1.0011.
According to the opinion of the State Council Office on Promoting the Development of Individual Pensions, the financial products in which the funds of the Individual Pension Fund Account can be invested include banking, savings deposits, commercial pension insurance, public funds, etc.
The first batch of individual pension fund management products was launched, marking that individual pension investors can officially purchase investment products through the individual pension fund account.
In November last year, the China Insurance Regulatory and Supervisory Commission formulated the “Interim Measures for the Management of Individual Pension Business of Commercial Banks and Wealth Management Companies”.
The Regulations provide that participants can purchase personal pension savings, personal pension wealth management products, personal pension insurance products, and personal pension open-end fund products through their individual pension funds accounts.
Thereafter, the Ministry of Human Resources and Social Security, the Ministry of Finance, and the State Taxation Administration jointly issued a notice to clarify that the personal pension system would be implemented in Beijing, Tianjin, and 36 other cities and regions including Shijiazhuang and Xiongan New Area in Shanxi Province.
As of December 31, 2022, there were 19.5 million participants in personal pension plans, with 6.13 million individuals contributing to them and total contributions amounting to RMB 1.42 billion.
Previously, the pilot banks only launched three types of products, namely individual retirement savings, individual retirement insurance and individual retirement fund.
Now that individual pension products have been aggregated, how should investors choose?
Experts from the Jilin Bank Product Development Department said that compared with other personal pension products, both pilot-stage pension-linked wealth management products and individual pension-linked wealth management products have three characteristics.
The first is stability, better risk management mechanisms, more robust investment strategies and concepts, and the implementation of independent third-party custody outside the parent bank.
II. Long-term nature, with most pilot phase pension products having maturities of five years or more; in the next issuance of individual pension products, the minimum holding period is generally one year, and encouraging a holding period of three years or more.
The third is accessibility, the product purchase threshold is low, the starting point is generally 1 yuan, some are as low as 0.01 yuan, the product handling fee, administration fee and other fees are more favorable.
Experts point out that investors should make their choices based on the product's characteristics and their own risk tolerance.
Individual pension savings have characteristics of long-term duration, high interest rates, and high safety, making them suitable for individuals with low risk tolerance; individual pension insurance products focus on protection, making them more appropriate for those who cannot bear investment risks but can accept stable returns; while individual pension product and open-end fund products do not guarantee returns or yields, they carry some investment risks, yet offer higher expected returns, which are more suitable for individuals with certain financial knowledge and higher risk tolerance.
Article/Reporter: Cheng Jie; Coordination: Chai Hua Bo
Newly Appointed Members of the Central Committee, Alternate Members, and Provincial and Ministerial Level Main Leaders Complete Study Course on Learning and Implementing Xi Jinping Thought on Socialism with Chinese Characteristics for a New Era and the 20th National Congress Spirit - Rolling News - Huasheng Online - Hunan Daily
Newly-elected members of the Politburo Standing Committee and alternate members as well as provincial and ministerial-level leading cadres have completed their study course on implementing Xi Jinping Thought on Socialism with Chinese Characteristics for a New Era and the 20th National Congress of the Communist Party of China.
2023-02-11 13:07:20 [Source: Xinhua News Agency] [Editor: Li Xufeng] [Font:【大 中 小】
Xinhua News Agency reported that the Central Committee’s new members and candidates for membership in the Politburo Standing Committee as well as provincial and ministerial-level leading cadres who have joined the Communist Party of China (CPC) at the 20th National Congress of the CPC were gathered to attend a seminar on learning and implementing Xi Jinping Thought on Socialism with Chinese Characteristics for a New Era and the spirit of the 20th CPC National Congress. The seminar concluded today afternoon at the Central Party School (National Academy of Governance), where General Secretary of the CPC Central Committee, Zhang Jie, attended the closing ceremony and delivered a speech summarizing the seminar.
He said that we should deeply study and implement the important speech of General Secretary Xi Jinping at the opening ceremony of the seminar, and more firmly adhere to the two major affirmations and the two major safeguards, strengthen our ability and do solid work to make solid progress in all aspects of building a socialist modern country in all-round construction of the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation, and create a performance that can stand the test of history, practice and the people.
During the training, all participants learned the spirit of the 20th CPC National Congress and the important speech delivered by General Secretary Xi Jinping at the opening ceremony of the training, and exchanged in-depth research and discussion on a series of major theoretical and practical issues of China's modernization, which strengthened their confidence and determination to carry out the great cause of the rejuvenation of the Chinese nation under the strong leadership of the CPC Central Committee with Chinese characteristics, and strengthened their sense of responsibility and mission to do a good job and ensure a good start in the new era.
At the graduation ceremony, 10 representatives made speeches and shared their learning experience.
Chai Qi stated that learning and implementing the thought of socialism with Chinese characteristics for a new era under Xi Jinping’s leadership is both an urgent political task for the present and in the future as well, and should be carried out according to the requirements of “comprehensive study, comprehensive grasp, and comprehensive implementation.” It is necessary to push forward the work on learning and implementing it further down deep, more solidly, and deeper into people's hearts.
To more deeply understand the decisive significance of “the two establishments,” we must resolutely uphold the core position of Xi Jinping and the authority of the Central Committee with Comrade Xi at its heart, as well as the centralized and unified leadership of the Party. We should continuously enhance our political judgment, political insight, and political execution, ensuring that we always maintain high consistency in thought, politics, and action with the Central Committee led by Comrade Xi.
To diligently master and apply Marxist theory as one’s forte, consciously arm oneself with the Party’s innovative theories to guide one’s thoughts, practice, and work, and strive to achieve deep study, meticulous understanding, and firm implementation in these areas; truly learn to acquire unwavering belief, absolute loyalty, and mission commitment.
To earnestly implement all decisions and deployments of the 20th National Congress of the Communist Party of China with an enterprising spirit, advance the Chinese-style modernization, roll up our sleeves to work hard, get down to business as a good “construction supervisor”, step by step turn the blueprint into reality.
It is imperative to remember that comprehensive and strict governance of the Party must be pursued at all times, and self-revolution within the Party must also continue forever. The political responsibility for comprehensive and strict governance of the Party should be pressed firmly, with party political construction serving as the overarching principle, and efforts should be made to advance the new great project of Party building in the new era.
To enhance skills in promoting high-quality development, serving the people, and managing risks, we must vigorously promote research work, resolutely prevent and correct formalism and bureaucracy.
Zhi Tai Feng, Li Ganjie, Li Shulei, Chen Wenqing, Liu JinGuo, Wang Xiaohong attended the graduation ceremony and Chen Xi presided over it.
The last communist premier of East Germany dies today
The successor party to the East German Communist Party reported in a statement that "last night Hans Modrow left us, aged 95."
As a result, our party has lost an important leader.
“
On 13 November 1989, four days after the opening of the Berlin Wall, which had separated East and West Berlin for 28 years, Moderro said he would help transform East Germany into a democratic state.
At the time, the Communist Party leaders were forced to step down as protesters across East Germany demanded democracy and freedom.
After the Soviet Union came to power, Mikhail Gorbachev called for changes in Soviet-dominated Eastern Europe as well.
On March 1990, Modrow announced the first and only free election of the German Democratic Republic (GDR).
The election result led to his no longer being prime minister.
Despite Modr's reforms, opponents accused him of trying to delay the political change and unification that took place in October 1990.
He has also been criticized for trying to reform the secret police rather than abolish it.
In 1993, Modro was convicted of electoral fraud in the May 1989 municipal elections, but was not jailed.
Some of the allegations were made for political reasons.
From 1990 to 1994, Modrow continued his parliamentary career in Germany and served as an MEP from 1999 to 2004.
Modro sees himself as a reformer and wants to change the Communist Party from within.
In 1999, he told Reuters that he did not want the former East Germany to return, but that it should be recognized for its achievements.
Modro was born in 1928 in the then German town of Jasenitz (now Jasienica, Poland) and trained as a mechanic.
During World War II, he served as a youth fire brigade leader and soon after the conflict ended as a member of the Volkssturm, a Nazi militia organization that recruited men aged 16 to 60 to fight in the final war struggles.
At the age of 17, Modro was captured by the Soviet army and taken as a prisoner of war to the Soviet Union, where he attended an anti-fascist course and became a staunch Communist Party member.
In 1949, the year East Germany was founded, he returned to the country and found a job as a mechanical engineer and continued his studies in social sciences and economics, earning a doctorate.
Modrow was a member of the Free German Youth movement, which almost all East German youth joined, and rose to become the head of the party in the Dresden region from 1973 to 1989 through the ruling Socialist Unity Party (SED).
He also served in the East German parliament for over 30 years.
In 1990, Modrow became de facto leader of East Germany and held the highest office in the country.
VNA Hanoi - VNA correspondents reported that the official visit to Singapore and Brunei by Vietnamese Prime Minister Pham Minh Chinh and his wife has been a complete success, yielding comprehensive, practical and specific results.
In the three days of his visit to Singapore and Brunei, Premier Feng Mingping attended more than 30 different events.
The results achieved have provided new impetus for the further development of the new strategic partnership between the two countries and the Vietnamese Comprehensive Partnership in a deeper, broader and more effective direction.
During his visit to the two countries, Prime Minister Pham Minh Chinh continued to reiterate the foreign policy of the Vietnamese Party and State, namely independence, diversity, flexibility, willingness to be a good friend and a reliable partner of all countries, and a responsible member of the international community.
Strengthening relations with Singapore and Brunei is in each country’s interest to promote the welfare of its people and contribute to regional and global peace, stability, and development.
During the meetings and discussions, Prime Minister Fan Minh Diem and the leaders of Singapore and Brunei agreed to continue to strengthen political mutual trust with Vietnam through high-level delegation visits and effective implementation of bilateral cooperation mechanisms and important cooperation agreements.
Many cooperation documents were signed during this visit.
Among these, two major highlights include the Memorandum of Understanding on Green and Digital Economy Partnership signed with Singapore and the Action Plan for Strengthening Comprehensive Partnership between Vietnam and Brunei Darussalam for the 2023-2027 Period.
Vietnam and Singapore sign a memorandum of understanding on green and digital economic partnership.
Photo credit: VNA
During meetings with business leaders, seminars or attendance at economic forums, PM Fan Minh Diem stressed that Vietnam welcomes and facilitates the expansion of investment in the fields of digital transformation, green energy, high technology, innovative innovation and other areas by Singaporean and Brunei enterprises.
This visit will not only help deepen the traditional cooperation between Vietnam, Singapore and Brunei in politics, diplomacy, economy, security, defense, education and training, oil and gas, tourism, and civilian exchanges, but also create a framework for cooperation in new potential areas such as digital economy, green economy, energy transition, innovation and creativity, smart cities, and sustainable development.
King Sultan Haji Hassanal Bolkiah of Brunei and Premier Wen Jiabao are preparing to enter a bilateral meeting.
Photo credit: VNA
During his visits to the two countries, Prime Minister Pham Minh Chinh arranged time to visit and listen to the thoughts and aspirations of the Vietnamese diaspora living in the two countries.
In meetings with their counterparts, Pham Minh Chinh called on both governments to pay more attention and create favorable conditions for fair treatment of local Vietnamese communities in both countries, so that they can contribute to society and nurture bilateral relations.
The proposal was approved and supported by the leaders of both countries.
In particular, Prime Minister Fan Mingyi also shared with the leaders of the two countries the desire for a united, peaceful, stable and prosperous ASEAN community; agreed to maintain united cooperation with ASEAN countries and enhance the central role of ASEAN in the complex and changing context of regional and international situations.
Based on the important results achieved, Prime Minister Fan Minh Diệm's official visits to Singapore and Brunei will contribute positively to the effective implementation of the 13th CPC General Assembly's priority foreign policy to strengthen relations with ASEAN neighbours, the effective implementation of the CPC Central Political Bureau's Conclusion No. 12 on Vietnam's work in the new situation ((12-KL/TW) and the development of the National Solidarity Force.
（End）
NEWS GOV-MO: Alert: Police Department urges citizens to be wary of fake text messages from telecom companies
Recently, the Police Bureau received multiple reports of telecommunications fraud cases where criminals impersonated local telecom companies and sent fraudulent SMSs containing links to fake websites, promising rewards for exchanging points that were about to expire.
The victim inputted the card information and verification code as instructed and received a notification from the financial institution that there were unidentified transactions on the credit card. He suspected that his credit card information had been stolen from the website.
After verification, it was confirmed that the relevant telecommunication company did not send the above short message.
The police department urges citizens to be vigilant when receiving such text messages, and not to log in to the website containing the text message or provide any personal information; if asked to provide credit card information, account transaction code, transaction verification code, be extra careful to prevent credit card theft.
Fraud Alert:
1. Pay more attention to cybersecurity news and enhance personal awareness of prevention.
Do not casually log onto unknown websites and register your personal and credit card information there to prevent identity theft;
3. Be vigilant against fake websites and phishing websites, and always check that the website addresses are in full compliance with the official website;
4. Install antivirus software on your mobile phone, computer, and update it regularly.
If you suspect that you have been a victim of fraud or any other crime, please contact the Police Commissioner's Fraud Reporting Hotline at 8800 7777 or the Crime Report Line at 993 for assistance immediately.
EU summit debates refugee policy, EU officials: the process of reception is stalled - China News
EU summit struggles over migrant policy, EU official: Every step of the process is a bottleneck
According to AFP, on February 10, at the latest EU summit of the day, EU Commission President Jean-Claude Juncker said that EU leaders agreed to a stricter policy on illegal immigration, which would make it easier to deport illegal immigrants.
The EU's move is reportedly in response to growing concerns about illegal immigration in Europe, where the EU's core problem is that few illegal immigrants are ultimately repatriated.
According to the summit document, EU leaders called on the Commission to immediately mobilize large amounts of EU funds to strengthen the external borders through infrastructure and surveillance.
However, the EU and its member countries are still at loggerheads over the cost of fencing.
Frauenfeld repeatedly stated that EU funds would not cover related costs.
But some diplomats from member countries said that if the EU could shoulder some of the cost of installing cameras, observation towers and other infrastructure along the external borders, it would free up national budgets to speed up construction.
The European Union’s Euractiv website reports that EU officials acknowledge that there are bottlenecks at every stage of the refugee reception process and that the limited capacity to receive refugees and member states’ overwhelmed immigration authorities cannot prevent refugees from submitting “numerous” asylum applications in all EU countries, putting the EU’s refugee reception system on an almost permanent crisis footing.
The European Commission estimates that in 2017, EU Schengen countries received over 920,000 asylum applications, up nearly half from the previous year.
Meanwhile, the EU recorded over 330,000 illegal entry cases last year.
In this context, the summit also agreed on a "principle" that EU member states can deport illegal immigrants to their home countries based on a court ruling of another member state.
In addition, the report said EU leaders also agreed to increase the use of the term "security state", which would pave the way for the EU to develop a common list.
(Source: Global Times; Author: Liu Ruifei)
Hsia Liuyan, vice chairman of the Kuomintang, conveyed Song Tao’s message that the 1992 Consensus is welcome for Green camp visits to China.
Taiwan’s Kuomintang Vice Chairman, Shieh Liang-ying, met with the Director of the Taiwan Affairs Office of the State Council, Song Tao, and the Politburo Member of the CPC Central Committee, Wang Huning, during his visit to China.
Senior Advisor Zhao Chunshan of the Nationalist Party’s official organization, the Council for Political and Economic Affairs, yesterday evening accepted an interview with Taiwan’s Central News Agency and actively praised Song Tao’s comments on Xia Liuyan that as long as one agrees to “the 92 Consensus” and anti-Taiwanese independence, China welcomes Green camp figures to visit mainland China.
The KMT side evaluated it as a new thing.
Xia Liyan met with Song Tao earlier that day, but the news did not mention this claim.
The ruling People's Democratic Party of Taiwan has repeatedly made clear that it does not accept the 1992 Consensus.
The Central News Agency reported today that Vice Chairman of the Kuomintang, Xia Liuyan, led an delegation to visit China, where he met with Standing Committee member of the CPC Politburo Wang Lianying and newly appointed Director-General of the Nationalist Affairs Office Song Tao in Beijing, as well as Mayor of Beijing Yin Li.
Xia Liying and Song Tao met to discuss the political foundation of the CPC and the anti-Taiwan independence, and Zhao Chunshan, a senior advisor of the Nationalist Party, said that the "92 Consensus" of the Nationalist Party was the original "92 Consensus".
Zhao Chunshan notes that this is different from his previous experiences at meetings.
Recently, I had a video conference with scholars from the mainland, and this time, I did not hear any scholars talking about the unification and the “anti-secession law”. Instead, I heard the restoration of exchanges and dialogues.
Liu Chunhan pointed out that the two sides are at risk of a bloody war and that mainland China hopes to communicate its intention to improve relations through the Kuomintang.
Because there is no mutual trust between the two sides, the other party still wants to do a good job for the Taiwanese, and the representative does not want to make the cross-strait relations worse.
Zhao Chunshan also said that Wang Huning also gave a personal instruction to Cang Tian to "fulfill their (the farmers and fishermen in Taiwan) demands" and that if the demands cannot be fully solved, they should handle them on a case-by-case basis.
The report did not mention whether the KMT visitor to the mainland directly mentioned the daily disruption of the Taiwanese border by Chinese military aircraft, the problem of farming and fishing in a few Taiwanese counties, or whether the interview with a reporter from the Central News Agency asked such questions.
What was the mysterious object that crashed in Alaska's airspace?
Confusing and contradictory, speculation rife.
The US military again deployed the most advanced US stealth fighter F-22 on Friday afternoon, shooting down an unidentified object flying over Alaska, USA.
The crash site is 10 miles off the coast of Alaska.
This is the second time the US has shot down an airborne object in less than a week.
A Chinese spy balloon was shot down over the US coast of South Carolina on Saturday, days after it was floating over US airspace.
The Pentagon said the second object, which first entered U.S. airspace on Thursday night, was tracked by the U.S. military as it moved over northeastern Alaska, flying at an altitude of 12,000 meters (40,000 feet), was about the size of a small car and much smaller than the Chinese spy balloon that was shot down earlier.
The Pentagon still believes that there is no evidence to suggest that this object can be controlled.
John Coby, White House National Security Council strategic communications coordinator, said Friday that while the exact nature of the object flying high in the sky is not clear, it poses a legitimate threat to the safety of civil aviation aircraft.
Kobe said that this object is different from the spy balloon discovered in the United States, which does not have an attached payload.
Kobe said, "We call it a 'thing' because that's the best description we can make of it right now."
President Biden listened to the Pentagon's advice before ordering the object to be shot down, and he was very cautious in making the decision, Corby added.
The official description of the object in the United States can be roughly summarized as: It was the size of a small car, without a handlebar, no suspension, and was flying at an altitude of about 10,000 meters.
But these data do not answer basic questions such as what this object is, which country it belongs to, and what mission it is performing.
Currently, much of the analysis and speculation online suggests that this may be another Chinese balloon.
It could be from China, like the spy balloon that invaded US airspace and the Chinese balloon that was hovering over Latin America, both of which are performing a mission in different locations.
And some have linked this “object” in Alaska to UFOs.
The US Newsweek report quoted former US Congressman Peter Meijer as tweeting on Friday that he really hoped the UFO was a spy balloon and not a legitimate UFO.
The irony of conflating extraterrestrial spacecraft with weather balloons is striking, but it does not warrant an interstellar conflict, he said.
Megan was posting the tweet shortly after Kobe confirmed the object was shot down over Alaska.
The newsweekly said that Major was not the only one to suspect the object of being a UFO.
Republican Representative Tim Burchett of Tennessee criticized the government's cover-up last month, demanding that the Office of the Director of National Intelligence (DNI) publish a report on the UFO sighting.
Xi Jinping's Letter to the Members of the Chinese Medical Team in Africa Encourages Them to Practice Compassionate Medicine to Benefit the Local People and to Tell the Story of China with Real Actions - News - Hunan Daily - Huanxi Shibao
Xi Jinping's letter to encourage China's medical teams in Africa to serve local people with compassion and skill, and tell China's story through concrete actions
2023-02-11 13:09:10 [Source: Xinhua News Agency] [Editor: Li Xufeng] [Font:【大 中 小】
Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, February 10 - General Secretary of the CPC Central Committee, President of the People's Republic of China and Chairman of the Central Military Commission Xi Jinping sent a letter to the 19th batch of medical team to the Central African Republic on February 9, expressing his greetings to them and all the medical teams abroad and making a sincere wish.
In his reply, Xi Jinping said that you have overcome difficulties in work and life in the Central African Republic, and have served the local people with your heart, and you are both a white angel of rescue and a friendly ambassador.
This year marks the 60th anniversary of China’s dispatching medical teams abroad; I extend sincere greetings to all comrades who have and continue to serve in international medical missions.
Xi Jinping pointed out that China’s people love peace and cherish life, which is vividly illustrated in medical aid missions abroad.
I hope you will not forget your first thoughts, remember your mission, and work hard to promote the spirit of the Chinese medical team, which is dedicated to sacrifice, rescue and relief, and loves no borders, to benefit the local people with kindness and charity, to tell the story of China with practical actions, and to make a greater contribution to promoting the construction of a community of human health and health.
Foreign medical assistance is an important component of China's foreign aid work.
In 1963, China sent its first medical team abroad to Algeria.
Over six decades, China has dispatched over 300,000 medical personnel to 76 countries and regions in Africa, Asia, America, Europe, and Oceania, treating more than 290 million patients, winning widespread acclaim from the international community.
Currently, the medical teams are working in 115 medical facilities in 56 countries around the world, with almost half of them in remote and difficult areas.
Recently, 11 members of the 19th batch of China’s medical teams dispatched to Central Africa wrote letters to President Xi Jinping, reporting on their efforts in implementing the spirit of the 20th CPC National Congress and providing medical services for local residents, as well as expressing their determination to contribute to building a community with a shared future for mankind.
Iranian revolution anniversary: Hacker supporting protests hijacks presidential speech
An official rally was held on Saturday to mark the 44th anniversary of the Islamic Revolution in Iran, but an anti-government hacker briefly interrupted a televised speech by President Ibrahim Raisi.
The president’s televised address was interrupted for about a minute on the Internet, and a group of Iranian hackers known as “Edalat Ali (Ali Justice)” appeared on screen.
There was also a voice shouting "Death to the Islamic Republic."
Reuters reports that Iran is commemorating its revolution anniversary and hackers have disrupted national TV broadcasts.
Iranian officials mark 44th anniversary of Islamic Revolution; Shiraz’s hardliners face biggest challenge yet from young protesters demanding their ouster but still urges “deceived youth” to repent so they can be pardoned by Iran’s supreme leader.
The wave of nationwide protests continues in Iran after the death of 22-year-old Mahsa Amini in September in the custody of the country's moral police.
The deadly crackdown on protests by Iranian security forces is one of the biggest challenges facing the Islamic Republic since the 1979 revolution that toppled the 2,500-year-old monarchy.
As part of an amnesty to commemorate the anniversary of the revolution, Iranian authorities released imprisoned dissidents Fahad Mesami and Iranian-French scholar Fariba Adelha on Friday for their hunger strike protests.
Earlier Ayatollah Ali Khamenei issued an amnesty decree that included some of those arrested during recent anti-government protests.
According to HRANA, 528 protesters have been killed as of Friday, including 71 minors.
The report said that 70 other government security personnel were killed.
According to reports, more than 19,763 protesters were arrested.
For weeks, Iranian leaders and state media have been calling for a vote at Saturday's rally to show opposition to the protests and support for the government.
Official media showed fireworks being used as part of government-sponsored celebrations on the anniversary of the Islamic revolution on Friday night, with people chanting "Allahu Akbar!"
God is the greatest!
However, many people at the rally were also heard shouting "Death to the dictator!"
and the "death of the Islamic State" videos posted on social media.
Saturday, the government TV broadcast live footage of official gatherings across all states.
In Tehran, as part of the official celebrations, domestic anti-ballistic missiles, drones, anti-submarine cruisers and other military equipment were displayed.
President Lies' speech is often interrupted by the "Death to America" chant - a signature chant at the rallies.
The crowd also chanted "Death to Israel."
Adelkhah, who has been in prison since 2019, is one of seven French nationals detained in Iran, Reuters said, a factor in the deterioration of relations between Paris and Tehran in recent months.
She was sentenced to five years in prison in 2020 on national security charges.
They later confined her at home but she returned to prison in January.
Adelkhah denied the allegations.
A week before Mesami was released, supporters warned that he was in danger of death as a result of the hunger strike.
He was arrested in 2018 for protesting the mandatory wearing of headscarves.
The French Foreign Ministry responded to Adelkhah's release on Friday, calling for her freedom to be restored, including the possibility of her being allowed to return to France if she wishes.
